Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:03.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What if every spider on Earth hunted together?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.70,0:00:04.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You are in bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.70,0:00:06.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Something moves in the corner.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.30,0:00:07.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then another.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.30,0:00:08.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}And another.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.80,0:00:09.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.50,0:00:12.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}There are over fifty thousand kinds of spiders.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.50,0:00:15.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Together they weigh about twenty-five million tons.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.50,0:00:20.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}And every year, they eat up to eight hundred million tons of prey.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.20,0:00:23.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}That's up to twice what all humans eat in meat and fish.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.90,0:00:29.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}If they ever worked as one… no forest, field or house would be safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.70,0:00:31.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.00,0:00:32.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Some spiders already do.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.70,0:00:40.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In the tropics of the Americas, thousands share one giant web… and take down prey far bigger than themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.80,0:00:41.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.80,0:00:45.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Without spiders, the world would be crawling with insects.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.40,0:00:46.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Maybe they're on our side.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.80,0:00:49.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Would you let one live in your house?
